      "body": "## Purpose\r\n\r\nCloses #45605\r\n\r\nRestores `vllm/tool_parsers/gemma4_utils.py` as a backward-compatible deprecated wrapper, rather than deleting it outright, to avoid breaking existing user code that imports `parse_tool_calls` or `has_tool_response_tag`.\r\n\r\nBoth functions now emit `DeprecationWarning` directing users to `tokenizer.parse_response()` from Transformers v5. Internal logic (regex tiers, `_parse_gemma4_args`) is unchanged.\r\n\r\nAlso updates the stale cross-reference in `vllm/reasoning/gemma4_utils.py` from `tokenizer.parse_chat_response()` to `tokenizer.parse_response()` from Transformers v5.\r\n\r\nNote: PR #39070 (bugfix on `gemma4_utils._parse_tool_arguments`) remains relevant since the file is now restored. PR #46475 (adds unit tests for utility modules) is unaffected.\r\n\r\nAI assistance was used in authoring this change.\r\n\r\n## Test Plan\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n# Verify import works cleanly\r\npython3 -c \"from vllm.tool_parsers.gemma4_utils import parse_tool_calls, has_tool_response_tag; print('OK')\"\r\n\r\n# Verify no broken references\r\ngrep -rn \"tool_parsers.gemma4_utils\" vllm/ --include=\"*.py\"\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Test Result\r\n\r\n```\r\n$ python3 -c \"from vllm.tool_parsers.gemma4_utils import parse_tool_calls, has_tool_response_tag; print('OK')\"\r\nOK\r\n\r\n$ grep -rn \"tool_parsers.gemma4_utils\" vllm/ --include=\"*.py\"\r\nvllm/tool_parsers/gemma4_utils.py:33:    from vllm.tool_parsers.gemma4_utils import (\r\nvllm/tool_parsers/gemma4_utils.py:118:        >>> from vllm.tool_parsers.gemma4_utils import parse_tool_calls\r\nvllm/tool_parsers/gemma4_utils.py:187:        >>> from vllm.tool_parsers.gemma4_utils import has_tool_response_tag\r\n```\r\n\r\nOnly self-references within the file itself — no external callers.",
      "changedFiles": 2,
